WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.040
- A mistrial is declared
in the California case

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.680
against Michael Avenatti.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.513
In this particular case,

00:00:04.513 --> 00:00:06.230
Michael Avenatti was cross-examining

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.403
a member of the Treasury Department

00:00:07.403 --> 00:00:09.170
and questioning why the government

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.243
didn't turn over specific accounting data

00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:13.330
to him and his defense team,

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.108
although those are sort of
one in the same at this point.

00:00:15.108 --> 00:00:17.210
Avenatti claimed that this
evidence was exculpatory

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.760
and integral to his defense

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.010
and that it was wrong for the government

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.680
to not turn it over
before the trial happened.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.541
The government said that
this data was effectively

00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.540
not important whatsoever
and was not exculpatory

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.410
but the judge agreed with Michael Avenatti

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.640
and declared a mistrial.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.240
That does not mean that
Michael Avenatti is going free.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.520
It just means that the government

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.860
will have to retry Michael Avenatti.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.700
A mistrial doesn't mean that
people go off scot-free.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.930
It just means that this trial
is declared null and void

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.960
and the government has
to do it all over again.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:45.793
The judge didn't think

00:00:45.793 --> 00:00:47.550
that the government had
committed any wrongdoing,

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.110
but they should have turned this data

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.140
over to Michael Avenatti.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.170
It was prejudicial.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.040
So we're gonna have to do
this whole thing over again,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.883
so I will see them in court.

